{arial}Sphinx Relay
Operator: Sergeant Barkod

from: {arialbld}Alex Kolman{arial}
Headquaters of Kapharna

to: {arialbld}{rank} {name}{arial}
Meknes Naval Base




Well {rank}, you've really wowed everybody with that stunning victory at El Getar, and I daresay the old Desert Fox owes you one now.  But don't let all the wild cheering around your jeep lull you into cloud-cuckoo land, because your head is lying right underneath a hanging anvil. That same jeep is just as popular with the Tektons - for target practice ... 

A severe shortage of oil is seriously endangering our campaign into the Jaffari interior.  At present we cannot provide for the full range of our equipment in action.   

We must take control of the oil wells in the Kataran Gulf. Don't bet on the Psychos kissing the ground you walk on when you fill our tankers. Two Tekton citadels hold control over the Gulf: {arialbld}Mostaganem{arial}, a wasp's nest of heavy armoured tanks and tactical bombers Otton sits on, and {arialbld}Ksar-El-Kebir{arial}, a major production center for battle cruisers, the jewels of Tankred's navy.


I unfortunately can't supply you with vessels that powerful, although Meknes has the resources to produce submarines ...














{center}{device21}

















You will be fighting jointly with the Fox's men. Kurt Rorscham has been sent to Molta. Depending on who you ask, he is preparing a landing on Cecily or he is trying to help people forget about him.  The infamous Schyzo media went wild over the Camel Derby incident; Tyron Spirex, Chief of the Schyzo forces, could really have lived without such publicity...


{offset150}{arialbld}Alex Kolman{arial}

Considerable Chief of the Normo Armies



